  "headline_finding": "On the original 3 parents (phenol scenario, 24 actions / 16 products), the agent had a clear advantage: greedy 0/3, random 3/9 qualifying products, agent 7/12 goal_met observations (toluene 4/4). On the 5 P1 parents (parent scenario, 70 actions / 40 products), the picture inverts: greedy 7 qualifying products across 3/5 parents (catechol, resorcinol, benzonitrile), random 7 across 4/5 parents (4-methylphenol, 4-fluorophenol, benzonitrile, catechol). The agent has only n=1 per P1 parent, so a single observation cannot establish a stable advantage; the earlier 'agent > random >> greedy' claim is true ONLY for the original 3 parents, not the extended 8-parent set.",
